From: j7
Subject: j7: find the desktop background by its own colour

The wallpaper never appeared, and the report line says why: "took 0 background pixels" on
every frame. The exact-black test and the near-black test both replace nothing, because the home
screen, the lock screen and the app switcher each paint their own dark colour and none of them is
(0,0,0).

Sample the layer that covers the display once per present, take its most common colour bucket,
and accept it only when it covers a fifth of the samples and is dark. A run of at least 32 pixels
of that colour, or of anything near-black, is background and takes the picture; a white app page
produces no background colour at all and is left alone.

Co-Authored-By: dipa-studio <183933817+dipa-studio@users.noreply.github.com>

